Client only, in roRouteReply's explain_blockers branch (Insights.tsx:520-525). Claim the gate's reasons only when there are some, and otherwise state the run's own recorded blockers from the server-rendered document. Do not re-derive the gate on the client.

```ts
const reasons = rep.truthfulness?.reasons ?? [];
const blockers = rep.sections.flatMap(s => s.blocks)
  .filter(b => b.kind === 'blocker-list')
  .flatMap(b => (b.items ?? []).map(String));
const label = rep.reportTypeLabel;
const text = reasons.length
  ? `"${label}" is held at ${rep.status}: ${reasons.join('; ')}. Those are the truthfulness gate's own reasons, verbatim.`
  : blockers.length
    ? `"${label}" is at ${rep.status} because its run recorded ${blockers.length} outstanding blocker${blockers.length > 1 ? 's' : ''}: ${blockers.join('; ')}. The truthfulness gate has not been asked for final on this run. Finalizing asks it, and a refusal states its reasons.`
    : `"${label}" is at ${rep.status}. Its run recorded no blockers and the truthfulness gate gave no reason.`;
```

The `blocker-list` section is what renderReport emits from run.blockers (render.ts:165-170). Drop "Clear them and it can promote toward final" from the no-reasons branches. Whether clearing blockers allows final depends on the type's rules: compliance.audit_assurance_pack has no requireBlockers, for example, and is held by requireExplicitGaps instead. Also correct the ROReport comment at :700-712 so it no longer says the band states what would move the report to final.
